{
 "idea": {
  "id": "weekday_season",
  "family": "calendar",
  "title": "Stocks that do well on a given weekday keep doing well on that weekday",
  "why": "Keloharju, Linnainmaa and Nyberg (2016) found that a stock's average return on, say, Mondays over past years predicts its return next Monday against other stocks, and likewise for every weekday. They tie it to recurring flows (weekly option expiries, payroll and fund flows that arrive on fixed days). It needs no news and resets every day, so the whole book turns over daily and cost decides it.",
  "source": "Keloharju, Linnainmaa, Nyberg 2016, Return seasonalities; Heston, Korajczyk, Sadka 2010 for the intraday form",
  "market": "us",
